# Local benchmark result store (figures, reward detail, run index).
# Results are data, not code: they stay on the machine that produced them.
results-local/
results/

# Agent scratch — ONE place: `.scratch/` at the root of the worktree you are
# working in. One-shot probe scripts, sweep logs, intermediate dumps.
#
# Anchored on purpose. Unanchored it would also bless a `.scratch/` inside a
# case directory, and `environment/` there is hashed into the case's container
# identity by Harbor whether git ignores it or not — so the ignore would hide
# from `tools/check_host_tree.py` exactly the class of file that tool exists to
# find. At the root there is nothing to hide from: no compared path reaches it.
#
# Per-worktree by construction, so parallel agents do not collide, and it is
# what #345 already used before it was ignored.
/.scratch/

# `/temp/` and `/tmp/` (above) are the same idea under two earlier names. They
# stay ignored as a net for old habits; neither is the convention any more.
/temp/

# A stale `python -m build` output tree was tracked here; the package is built
# from source, so the copy only ever drifted.
lib/*/build/

# Agent worktrees: real git worktrees, tracked by git itself, never content.
.claude/worktrees/


# The board deploy stamp: written by `check_board_deploy.py --write-stamp`
# immediately before the rsync that carries it, so the host can name the commit
# it is serving (#534 item 5). Per-deploy, not per-commit -- it records what was
# shipped, which is exactly the fact a tracked file could not carry.
deploy/hwe-bench-log/.deploy-stamp.json
